                <invention-title lang="de">VERFAHREN ZUM SENDEN/EMPFANGEN BIOMETRISCHER INFORMATIONEN OHNE VERLUST IN EINEM KONTINUIERLICHEN GLUCOSEÜBERWACHUNGSSYSTEM</invention-title>
                <invention-title lang="fr">PROCÉDÉ DE TRANSMISSION/RÉCEPTION D'INFORMATIONS BIOMÉTRIQUES SANS PERTE DANS UN SYSTÈME DE SURVEILLANCE CONTINUE DU GLUCOSE</invention-title>
                <invention-title lang="en">METHOD FOR TRANSMITTING/RECEIVING BIOMETRIC INFORMATION WITHOUT LOSS IN CONTINUOUS GLUCOSE MONITORING SYSTEM</invention-title>
            </bibliographic-data>
            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>The present disclosure relates to a method for transmitting or receiving biometric information in a continuous glucose monitoring system and, more specifically, to a method for transmitting or receiving biometric information, in which: when a sensor transmitter generates a transmission packet, the transmission packet is generated to include a generation identifier for identifying the transmission packet or biometric information according to a generation order of the transmission packet or the biometric information, and therefore the biometric information may be transmitted or received without a loss thereof via the generation identifier; and a transmission packet or biometric information, which a communication terminal has failed to receive, is correctly determined on the basis of a packet generation identifier or a total number of transmission packets, so that only biometric information or a transmission packet, which has failed to be received between the sensor transmitter and the communication terminal, may be transmitted or received in a distinguished manner.</p>
            </abstract>
